Overall Comparison: Of these three careers, Information Security Analyst interests me the most
because it directly connects to the Cybersecurity degree I am working toward and has strong
future growth. Network and Computer Systems Administrator also interests me because it is
more hands-on and could provide a strong technical foundation for cybersecurity. Security
Manager fits my previous leadership experience and could become a long-term goal after I gain
more technical experience.
The strongest career path for me could be:
Network/IT experience → Information Security Analyst → Cybersecurity or Security
Management
That path would allow me to combine my hands-on ability, military leadership experience,
cybersecurity education, and interest in eventually moving into management.
